# What must NOT be uploaded to the deployment.
#
# Vercel serves this repo's root as the static site, so anything committed here is
# reachable at https://www.digidental.us/<path> unless it is listed below. That was
# already true while the repo was private — the deployment never cared about GitHub
# visibility — so /supabase/APPLY_TO_SUPABASE.sql and /test/security.test.mjs were
# fetchable by anyone who guessed the path. Making the repo public did not create the
# exposure; it removed the guessing.
#
# None of this is a credential leak: every key in these files is either a browser key
# that ships in dd-logic.js anyway, or a `process.env` reference. It is the full
# database schema, the RLS policies and the security test suite being served off the
# marketing domain, which tells an attacker exactly what to probe for free.
#
# Nothing here is read at runtime. There is no `build` script in package.json, so
# Vercel runs no build step and excluding the test suite cannot break one. api/,
# lib/, package.json, vercel.json and every asset the pages reference are all
# deliberately absent from this list.

# Database schema, RLS policies and migrations — applied by hand in the Supabase
# dashboard, never by the deployment.
supabase/

# Test suites. They run in CI and locally, against the repo, never against the deploy.
test/

# Local maintenance scripts (npm run seo:submit).
scripts/

# Internal docs: open TODOs, launch checklist, the things still awaiting legal review.
# Public on GitHub on purpose; no reason to also serve them from the sales domain.
README.md
SEO-LAUNCH-CHECKLIST.md

# Variable names only, no values — but there is nothing for a visitor here either.
.env.example

# Repo tooling and a stray editor artefact.
.github/
.thumbnail
.gitignore
